# Subway Train: the {G} is optional ("you may pay"). With Mox Emerald's {G} in the pool Bot1 declines, so nothing is searched or shuffled: the library
# is still 13 cards with the Forest in it and the {G} stays in the pool. Then "Crew 2": a lone Zephyr Sprite (power 1) cannot crew it (the refusal, the
# Vehicle still a plain artifact); with a second Sprite the two together (total power 2, exactly) crew it and it becomes an artifact creature.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Subway Train
Zephyr Sprite
Zephyr Sprite
Forest
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Subway Train.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Decline
? Bot1.Library.Count = 13
? Bot1.Mana = {G}
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Zephyr Sprite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Subway Train.Activate(Ability: Crew)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Zephyr Sprite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Subway Train.Activate(Ability: Crew)
Bot1.Choose(Zephyr Sprite#1; Zephyr Sprite#2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Subway Train.Types.Count = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Zephyr Sprite#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Zephyr Sprite#2.Tapped = true
